@* card.md §2.6 (right panel) / §3.9: the prototype seeds a 7-month delta bar row, a
   gem-rate sentence, and a pace sentence, but Phase 2's CensusDto carries no deltas --
   only the fixed six bars and QualifyingObservations. §3.9's own LOW DATA rule
   ("< 2 census observations") always applies today: the 2026-09-01 floor (D-033)
   means no card has two qualifying observations yet.

   D-087 applied (owner, 2026-08-13): the mockup's two metric rows render as SLOTS
   holding LOW DATA states that name their unlock condition -- the panel keeps the
   finished product's geometry. Rule 2 boundary: these are states, never placeholder
   numbers; the numbers themselves arrive with the worker phase's delta substrate. *@
@using CardStock.Application.Cards

<div class="activity-panel">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <h2>Grading activity · PSA 10 slabs added</h2>
        <span class="obs-badge" title="@BadgeTooltip()">@(Census.QualifyingObservations) OBS</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ga-metric">
        <span class="ga-metric-name">Gem rate</span>
        <span class="ga-state">LOW DATA</span>
        <span class="ga-metric-note">@UnlockNote()</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ga-metric">
        <span class="ga-metric-name">Pace</span>
        <span class="ga-state">LOW DATA</span>
        <span class="ga-metric-note">@UnlockNote()</span>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public CensusDto Census { get; set; } = default!;

    private string BadgeTooltip() =>
        $"Census observations counted from 2026-09-01 — {Census.QualifyingObservations} so far; deltas need two.";

    private string UnlockNote() =>
        $"needs census deltas; observations count from 2026-09-01, {Census.QualifyingObservations} so far — deltas need two";
}
